      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to avoid potassium supplements while taking lisinopril, as this medication can raise your potassium levels, and adding more could lead to dangerous hyperkalemia. The leg cramps are a known side effect of lisinopril, so please contact your prescribing doctor—they may adjust your dose or suggest a different medication. Do not start any potassium or salt substitutes without speaking to your healthcare provider first.",
