      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Coconut water is actually a significant source of potassium, so drinking it while on lisinopril carries the same risk as a pill—your kidneys are already retaining potassium, and any extra can push you toward dangerous hyperkalemia. The only truly safe, non-doctor fixes for the cramps are physical measures: gentle calf stretches before bed, staying well-hydrated with plain water, and applying a warm compress to the muscles. Please don't risk a heart arrhythmia to avoid a phone call—your doctor can quickly order a simple blood test or switch you to a different BP medication that doesn't cause cramps.",
      "source": "target",
